# Environment variables for the IGA site.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development. `.env` is gitignored — never commit it.
# In production these are set in the Netlify UI:
#   Netlify -> Site configuration -> Environment variables
#
# Both are PUBLIC_ prefixed because Astro only exposes prefixed variables to
# client-side code. Neither is a secret: the GTM container ID is visible in the
# page source of every site that uses one, by design.


# --- Search-engine gate -----------------------------------------------------
# Unset (or anything other than exactly "true") = every page is noindexed.
# Fails safe: the wrong-way failure is an invisible site, not an accidentally
# indexed staging URL.
#
# >>> AT LAUNCH: set this to true in Netlify and redeploy. That's the whole step.
#
# PUBLIC_LAUNCHED=true


# --- Google Tag Manager -----------------------------------------------------
# The container ID, format GTM-XXXXXXX. Unset = no GTM, no analytics, and no
# request to Google at all — which is what you want for `npm run dev`.
#
# Deliberately SEPARATE from PUBLIC_LAUNCHED so conversion tracking can be
# tested and proven before launch, while the site is still hidden from search.
# Every tag (GA4, Google Ads, Meta, Microsoft UET) is configured inside the GTM
# container, so adding a platform never requires a code change.
#
# The GA4 measurement ID (G-XXXXXXXXXX) does NOT go here — it is entered in the
# GTM container's GA4 tag.
#
# PUBLIC_GTM_ID=GTM-XXXXXXX
